<title>UK: Reed rebounds as Panmure says buy.</title>
<headline>Reed rebounds as Panmure says buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in publisher Reed International rebounded on Wednesday after brokers Panmure Gordon recommended that its clients buy the stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1217 GMT, the shares had added 12-1/2p to 1126p, after setting a three-month low on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We've liked Reed on a long-term basis for a long time, but put a hold on the shares when they got near 12 pounds. Now they've slipped into the buy range,&quot; said Anthony DeLarrinaga, a media analyst with Panmure.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
